CarbonCare InnoLab (CCIL) is registered under the laws of Hong Kong as a non-profit making and tax exempt charity. CCIL aims at nurturing and expanding an active community for climate justice. It is actively engaging NGOs, business, policy makers, the youths for achieving just transition to a low carbon economy where vulnerable communities will be respected and protected.
Programme Officer (Youth Empowerment)
We are looking for a passionate and enthusiastic individual who aligns with our values and initiatives and is ready to contribute to building a more sustainable Hong Kong with a just transition. We require a self-motivated and resourceful person who can support current projects as well as contribute to the organisation’s future growth.
Website: www.ccinnolab.org
KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:
• Assist, lead, organise and implement climate education programmes;

• Support programme activities and stakeholder engagement events and support;

• Develop and maintain partnership with international and/or local trust, foundation, institutions, NGOs, supporting organisations for effective programme operations;

• Cultivate and sustain networks with programme participants to ensure ongoing engagement and impact;

• Prepare promotion materials and other communications for social media or website to raise awareness and support CCIL's initiatives;

• Conduct data collection, compile report and analyse the impact of the programmes;

• Perform ad-hoc duties required by the Management.

QUALIFICATION AND EXPERIENCE:
• Preferably 2 years’ relevant working experience in NGOs, particularly in climate, education and youth empowerment related programmes. Fresh university graduates will also be considered if track records in extracurricular activities are provided.

• Strong passion for climate change, sustainability, and youth empowerment, with relevant work experience considered a significant advantage;

• Proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese (Fluent Cantonese is a must);

• Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage effectively with all levels of project stakeholders;

• Strong organisational abilities, multi-tasking skills and attention to details, with the capacity to work independently and under pressure;

• A team player with a collaborative mindset, able to work effectively with colleagues and partners to achieve common goals;

• Self-motivate, eager to explore, learn and share knowledge on related issues;

• Proficiency in using multimedia production software (Photoshop, Illustrator, Canva) and social media applications is preferable.

Salary package with fringe benefits will be commensurate with the qualification and experience of the successful candidate.
If you are ready to take on this exciting challenge and contribute to building a more sustainable future with CCIL, please email your full CV, portfolio, expected salary with the position title as the subject line to the Senior Programme Manager of CarbonCare InnoLab at adm••@ccinnolab.org
