M+ is a museum dedicated to collecting, exhibiting, and interpreting visual art, design and architecture, moving image, and Hong Kong visual culture of the twentieth and twenty-first centuries. Located in Hong Kong’s WestK, we are one of the leading museums of modern and contemporary visual culture in the world. The museum reflects our unique time and place, building on Hong Kong’s historic balance of the local and the international to define a distinctive and innovative voice for Asia’s twenty-first century. 

The M+ Internship Programme is a unique opportunity for those who are interested in developing a career in the museum field. You will work closely with the M+ team full time for a period of one year, gaining both practical and theoretical training. This intake will take place from September 2026 to August 2027.

The Publishing Internship offers hands-on experience in producing books and other print publications related to M+ collections and exhibitions. Under the mentorship of the publishing team, you will contribute to the creation of enduring content channels that grow the museum’s most dedicated audience, deepen art historical research, and enhance the museum’s reputation at home and abroad.

You will be able to:

learn about M+, its exhibitions, collections, books, and other programmes;

participate in content planning and creative brainstorming, focusing on books related to M+, its collections, exhibitions, and programmes;

gain a unique insight into the experience of working collaboratively as part of a multidisciplinary team;

assist in planning, researching, executing, and coordinating publishing projects;

perform any other duties from time to time as reasonably assigned by M+.

You need to:

possess a recognised university degree or equivalent qualification in art, curatorial studies, publishing, language studies, design history, architecture, film or media studies, art education, cultural studies, museum studies, or related subjects in humanities;

have strong interest in working in publishing, art, and culture industries;

possess strong communication and project management skills;

have strong organisational skills and be detail-oriented;

have strong teamwork and interpersonal skills;

demonstrate a strong interest in art-related publishing and its marketing; and

have a good command of spoken and written English and Chinese (Cantonese / Mandarin).
 

Please submit your application on or before 29 May 2026 via online application.  

