Supporting in contributing to and developing big-picture strategies to help the museum reach and grow wider audiences not only in Hong Kong but also regionally and internationally (such as Greater Bay area and Mainland China);

Managing the content calendar and overseeing publication of all informational and programming-related content for various M+ platforms such as the museum website;

Developing compelling ways to enhance the public’s understanding and awareness of the museum and subsequently deepen engagement;

Expanding the museum’s audience reach by exploring new platforms and opportunities, external partnerships or other initiatives;

Establishing and maintaining content publishing workflows, best practices and policies to ensure editorial consistency and accessibility across media and platforms;

Collaborating with the museum’s digital content, marketing, editorial, communications, and social media colleagues to sync messaging and marketing activities;

Managing and steering the work copywriter(s), editor(s) and translator(s) to ensure that draft content from individual teams is transformed into publishable, web-ready copy consistent with the M+ voice and style guidelines;

Reviewing data and analytics to harness insights and make data-driven decisions to expand the museum’s reach and impact online;

Working with in-house and external design and technology teams to maintain and iterate on digital content experiences and contribute to a roadmap for future enhancements;

Undertaking any other job duties as assigned; and

performing any duties from time to time as reasonably as assigned by M+.

You should:

Possess a recognised university degree, preferably in communications, journalism, translation, or related disciplines;

Have around 6-10 years of work experience in high-traffic digital content production environment either in arts or cultural organisations, or content-led organisations such as media and journalism with 3 years in supervisory role

Have prior experience in managing in-house and external content contributors and delivering online publishing or digital projects;

Have deep understanding of digital landscape and interest in new trends, technologies and behaviours of audiences online (especially in Hong Kong and Mainland China);

Have strong interpersonal skills and superb written skills in English;

Possess excellent Chinese reading and writing skills, with experience localising Chinese content;

Have strong project management skills and a keen eye for detail; and

be able to work well under pressure and deliver to tight deadlines.

