·Create and execute the digital marketing and promotion plan for engaging the target users and fundraising campaigns;

·Delivering effective communications activities including social media, eDMs and website with different stakeholders;

·Maintain, edit and generate engaging content, visual graphics, images and videos on all online platforms for organization’s activities and public education, including: Facebook, Instagram, Youtube, Website, Threads and others;

·Develop, design and produce marketing flyers, publications, souvenirs, annual report etc. Design Chairty Sales items, event souvenirs and certificates. Work with vendors for the production of publications.

·Build and maintain media relations with other medias, KOLs, artists and celebrities;

·Consolidate communication and promotional materials such as news clippings and others;

·Assist volunteer recruitment and engagement activities to support photos and video taking

·Basic office and event’s visual, IT and audio support;

Requirements  

·Diploma holder in communications, public relation, marketing or other relevant subjects;

·Basic knowledge of Photography, Canva, Adobe Illustrator, Photoshop and Premiere Pro is a plus

·Basic knowledge in website management, editorial skills, digital marketing;

·Good in MS office including Word, Excel, PowerPoint;

·Good communication and writing skills (English and Chinese);

·Detail oriented, well-organized, analytical mind and able to work with deadlines;

·Outgoing personality and passionate in the charity sector;

·Work flexibly including weekends and public holidays;

·Immediately available or short-noticing period is preferred.

THE ROLE
The Marketing Officer is a proactive, organised and professional individual responsible for supporting the efficient and successful management of pupil recruitment initiatives while promoting the ethos and philosophy of Malvern College Hong Kong. The incumbent will assist the Marketing Manager and Communications Manager in delivering effective services within the Marketing Team, ensuring alignment with the Malvern’s strategic goals.

RESPONSIBILITIES

Support Marketing Initiatives: Collaborate with the Marketing Manager and Communications Manager to support marketing eff orts aimed at achieving target enrolments, school objectives, and enhancing brand visibility.

Event Management: Assist in the planning, coordination, and execution of marketing-related events, such as Malvern Meets, fairs, networking events, workshops, and open days.

Logistics and Material Preparation: Prepare for events by packing and unpacking materials, setting up venues, and coordinating logistics to ensure seamless execution.

Liaising with Prospective Parents: Engage with prospective parents during events to provide information, answer questions, and foster connections, ensuring a welcoming environment that promotes engagement with the school community.

Digital Marketing Campaigns: Support the development and implementation of digital marketing campaigns to drive engagement and increase visibility across various platforms.

Website and Social Media Management: Manage and update the school’s website, social media platforms, and other publications, while tracking SEO performance and website traffi c to provide regular internal reports.

Data Collection and Analysis: Collect and analyse relevant market data, track digital engagement metrics, and provide insights to inform marketing strategies.

Content Creation: Support the Marketing Manager by utilising graphic design software and other tools to design and produce captivating marketing materials, including EDMs, advertisements, web banners, leafl ets, fl yers, brochures, and videos.

Community Engagement: Communicate with prospective families via phone, email, and in-person interactions to provide information and support regarding school event registration.

General Administrative Duties: Perform administrative tasks related to the marketing department, ensuring smooth operations and effi cient workfl ow.

Ad Hoc Responsibilities: Undertake any other duties as required by the Marketing Manager or Communications Manager to support departmental objectives.

REQUIREMENTS

Holder of Bachelor’s Degree preferable in communications, marketing, or a related field;

Good command of English;

At least 2 Years of working experience in marketing, preferably in the education sector, but this is not essential;

A positive attitude is essential and contributes to promoting a positive office culture within the organisation;

Convey enthusiasm with sincerity and consistency, with a proven track record of success in meeting targets, and be a highly motivated individual;

Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work both independently and as part of a team;

An organised individual with excellent time management skills to effectively juggle multiple tasks and priorities;

Understanding and experience with Adobe Suite software is desirable – i.e. Photoshop, Illustrator, etc.

Proficient in Canva and MS Office;

Knowledge of Google Analytics and SEO is advantageous;

Excellent customer service skills;

A desire to work in a fast-paced environment with the ability to multitask;

Good IT and administrative skills, with the ability to accurately utilise a large database.

HOW TO APPLY 

Please send the application with a cover letter and full resume including your current and expected salaries addressed to the Human Resources Department, Malvern College Hong Kong by clicking “Quick apply”.

Personal data provided by job applicants will be treated in strict confidence for recruitment purposes only. Please note that only shortlisted candidates will be invited for interviews. The final employment will be subject to pre-employment and child protection checks. 

