About the role

Ming Hing-CY Joint Venture is seeking a Public Liaison Manager to join our Public Relations & Corporate Affairs team. This is a full-time position based in Kowloon Bay, Kwun Tong District. In this strategic role, you will serve as a key bridge between our organisation and the public, managing communications, stakeholder relationships, and public perception. The Public Liaison Manager is essential to maintaining and enhancing our corporate reputation, ensuring clear and consistent messaging, and fostering positive relationships with all external stakeholders.

What you'll be doing

To station at office to operate on a 24/7 rotating shift basis to develop ad-hoc contents and posts for website and social media platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, WeChat, etc.;

To attend outdoor sites to conduct photo taking and video filming;

To track news reports, press clipping, and online narratives;

To regularly update the public relations-related content and announcement on the website and social media platforms;

To monitor and manage feedback on social media platforms;

To prepare regular reports on performance of social media platforms;

To undertake researches with a view to developing suitable contents for the social media platforms; and monitor trends in social media tools, applications, channels, design and public relations strategy;

To provide support to publicity and promotional events;

To provide support in liaising with the media; and

To take up other public relations-related duties as required.

What we're looking for

Have a degree from a Hong Kong university, or equivalent; preferably in Communications, Public Relations and Journalism [See Note (1)];

Have at least three years’ relevant post-qualification experience; preferably in the fields of journalism, publicity and public relations, and relevant fields;

have met the language proficiency requirements of Level 2 results in two language papers (Use of Chinese (“UC”) and Use of English (“UE”) in the Common Recruitment Examination (“CRE”) (or equivalent results) [See Note (2)];

have good understanding of political and/or community affairs;

possess strong communication, organization and presentation skills;

be self-motivated, mature and able to work independently and efficiently under pressure; and prepared to work irregular hours, including overnight shifts, weekends, and public holidays; and

excellent skills in photo-taking and editing for publishing on website and social media platforms such as Facebook, Instagram and WeChat.

Note:

Holders of academic qualifications other than those obtained from Hong Kong institutions / Hong Kong Examinations and Assessment Authority may also apply but their qualifications will be subject to assessments on equivalence with the required entry qualifications.  They should attach copies of their official transcripts and certificates of studies to their applications.

For appointment purpose, Level 5 or above in English Language of the Hong Kong Diploma of Secondary Education Examination (“HKDSEE”); or Grade C or above in Use of English of the Hong Kong Advanced Level Examination (“HKALE”); or Grade C or above in English Language of the General Certificate of Education (Advanced Level) (“GCE A Level”), are accepted as equivalent to Level 2 in the UE paper of the CRE. Level 5 or above in Chinese Language of the HKDSEE; or Grade C or above in Chinese Language and Culture or Chinese Language and Literature of the HKALE, are accepted as equivalent to Level 2 in the UC paper of the CRE. An overall band of 6.5 or above with no subtest score below band 6 obtained in the same sitting in the Academic Module of the International English Language Testing System (“IELTS”) within the two-year validity period of the test result is accepted as equivalent to Level 2 in the UE paper of the CRE. The IELTS test result must be valid on any date during the application period.

