Temporary Research Assistant I/Research Assistant II/Technical Assistant (R6565) (S&T) (Ref: 26001MA)

Major Duties and Responsibilities 

The appointee will mainly assist the research team in a research project “Development of Using Retired Batteries from Electrical Vehicles to Build Smart Emergency Power Systems for Buildings in Hong Kong” (R6565).  The appointee will be responsible mainly for the following:

Designing and validating coupled multi-physics models for agrivoltaics-wind systems under subtropical microclimates;

Deploying IoT-enabled smart monitoring systems for crops, livestock, and renewable energy generation;

Implementing machine learning algorithms to optimize energy generation, agricultural productivity, and cost-efficiency;

Conducting experiments and collecting data using IoT sensors (e.g., soil moisture, solar irradiance, wind speed);

Optimizing resource allocation (e.g., sunlight, ventilation) between energy and agricultural outputs;

Collaborating effectively with cross-disciplinary teams, including engineers, agronomists, and economists; and

Maintaining detailed documentation of system configurations and operational procedures, and publishing research findings in peer-reviewed conferences and journals.

