At least 5 subjects with Level 2 in HKDSE or equivalent, including English & Chinese languages and Mathematics / Diploma (for Technical Assistant);

A bachelor’s degree in Engineering (Electrical/Mechanical/Agricultural), Computer Science, Environmental Science, or a related discipline; (for Research Assistant II);

A master’s degree in Engineering (Electrical/Mechanical/Agricultural), Computer Science, Environmental Science, or a related discipline; (for Research Assistant I);

Candidates with prior research experience in IoT, renewable energy, or smart agriculture are highly desirable;

Candidates with the following skills are preferred;

Programming: Python, MATLAB, or C++ for modelling and data analysis;

IoT & Hardware: Sensor networks, Arduino/Raspberry Pi, and wireless protocols (LoRa, ZigBee, NB-IoT);

Data Analytics: Machine learning frameworks (TensorFlow, scikit-learn) and statistical tools (R, Excel); 

Domain Knowledge: Familiarity with photovoltaic systems, wind energy, and agricultural microclimates;

Strong communication skills, with the ability to effectively convey technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders;

A strong sense of responsibility, coupled with effective organizational and interpersonal skills; and

Proficiency in both English and Chinese.

