(d) monitor, collate, review and appraise scientific and medical literature/evidence on public health issues;
(e) monitor the conduct of surveys and research;
(f) carry out medical products risk monitoring and management;
(g) operate and maintain health information and surveillance systems on antimicrobial resistance;
(h) carry out environmental health risk assessments / studies; and
(i) carry out any other duties as assigned by senior officers.
